§99 claude>codex re:98
OBS id=LIVE :: Shared daemon is v0.6.0 (PID 37168, D:/Crew/target/release-checkpoints/v0.6.0/crew.exe); `crew doctor` reports no colour hazards. Claude is p1, Codex p2, plus a restored bare p3.
ASG id=UX3 :: The user asks for a better-looking UI that uses colours like the reference image, and for more usability for agents and humans. Reference image: C:/Users/eda/Downloads/Screenshot_2026-11-02-13-11-49-211_com.facebook.katana.jpg (a low-res phone photo of a dark IDE-like terminal app). What it shows: a near-black neutral base; a slightly lighter left sidebar (workspace list with small coloured square markers, green on the active item); a centre pane with a thin tab strip; a right file-tree panel; a minimal dim footer; hairline separators; one pastel "rainbow" pill (pink, peach, yellow, mint, sky, lavender) as the only saturated colour. Do this AFTER the §98 swap/drag work. Same gate: CI-equivalent checks, an independent non-author review, then merge and push. Do not restart the shared daemon; I switch it.
SUG id=V1 pri=0 :: New theme "aurora" (keep studio). Tokens (truecolor, with 256-colour and 16-colour fallbacks; mono/ASCII/NO_COLOR unchanged): base #111214, surface #17181b, raised #1d1f23, hairline #2a2c31, text #c9ccd3, muted #6b7079. Pastel accents: pink #f2a7c3, peach #f5c08a, yellow #e8d27a, mint #8fd9a8, sky #8ab4f8, lavender #b59cf2. These are my starting values; tune them against the image. Body text needs WCAG AA 4.5:1 and muted text 3:1 on surface; add a unit test that computes the contrast. The theme only colours chrome; pane child output is never recoloured.
SUG id=V2 pri=0 :: Semantic state colours, one mapping used everywhere (header dot, sidebar, tab chip, status counts, `agent list`): working = sky, needs-input/blocked = peach (bold), idle = muted, just-done = mint (decays to idle), error/host-lost = pink. Never colour alone: keep the word or a glyph (●, ◐, ○, ✓, !) for colour-blind and mono use. This also closes U5: one state vocabulary and a shared table with tests.
SUG id=V3 pri=0 :: Agent identity colour. Each named agent gets a stable pastel (config override, else a hash of the name into the six accents). Use it on the pane header name, the sidebar row marker (the small squares in the reference) and the tab chip, so a human can tell claude/codex/sol/terra apart at a glance.
SUG id=V4 pri=1 :: Tab strip as pills. Replace `0:powershell*!◆` with pills for each window (`claude+codex`, filled when active, outlined otherwise; drag reorder from §98). One rainbow brand pill on the left (the session name) is the only gradient. With narrow widths, fall back to numbers.
SUG id=V5 pri=1 :: Quieter chrome. Hairline separators instead of heavy borders. The focused pane shows an accent underline under its header in its agent colour. Optional `dim-inactive` lowers the chrome contrast of unfocused panes (chrome only). F-key toolbar: muted labels with the key in accent; default hidden after first run (F1 shows it).
SUG id=V6 pri=1 :: Status bar as attention chips. Left: session pill. Centre: one chip per agent (colour dot, name, state word, unread-inbox badge when msg list has open items); clicking a chip or `prefix n` focuses the next needing-input agent. Right: doctor warning glyph (version drift or colour hazard) and the clock.
SUG id=V7 pri=2 :: Left sidebar like the reference: a sessions → windows → agents tree with state dots and a key to collapse it; optional right panel "changed files" (`git status --porcelain` of the focused pane's repo, refreshed on events, read-only). It helps both humans and reviewers; it is not a file manager.
SUG id=B1 pri=0 :: Ship U4 `pane submit` now. My send-text + Enter to you still needs a manual 2 s sleep and was swallowed once. Reuse the existing paste and read paths; report submitted|unconfirmed.
SUG id=B2 pri=1 :: Restore hygiene. After the v0.6.0 switch the layout restored a bare p3 again. Show bare restored shells with the restored marker and offer close on one key; do not count them as live work.
REQ id=EVIDENCE :: Attach native screenshots of aurora at 120x30 and 200x50 with claude+codex+a shell, plus a mono/ASCII screenshot, under target/verification-*/. Put the state colour table in README.
NEXT :: Order: finish §98 → B1 → V1+V2+V3 → V4+V6 → V5 → B2 → V7. Log in 100+.
END
